<title>ITALY: Italian CPI 1.7 pct in April - Istat.</title>
<headline>Italian CPI 1.7 pct in April - Istat.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1997-05-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>The National Statistics Office (ISTAT) reported the following consumer inflation details:</p>
<p> ITALIAN INFLATION	   April 97  March 97     April 96</p>
<p> Monthly CPI index rise	 0.1	  0.1	  0.6</p>
<p> Yr-on-yr inflation	     1.7	  2.2	  4.5</p>
<p> Index (Base 1996)	    105.4	105.3	103.6</p>
<p>Istat said that including tobacco costs in the inflation data gave a CPI rate of 1.7 percent for April.  </p>
<p>ISTAT gave the following sector-by-sector breakdown.</p>
<p> Sector			   Index	   mo/mo (%)    yr/yr (%)</p>
<p> Food (without tabacco)     104.1	    0.0	   0.4</p>
<p> Clothing			 106.6	    0.4	   2.7</p>
<p> Housing,Electricity,Fuel   109.4	    0.6	   3.9</p>
<p> Domestic goods		 105.1	    0.0	   1.8</p>
<p> Health spending		105.6	    0.1	   3.0</p>
<p> Transport			105.9	   -0.1	   1.6</p>
<p> Recreation		     103.4	    0.0	   0.6</p>
<p> Education			107.4	   -0.1	   3.3</p>
<p> Hotels, restaurants	  106.1	    0.2	   2.6</p>
<p> Other goods,services	 103.7	    0.1	   1.0</p>
</text>
